": \"text\", \"document_id\": \"0745ef188a9c11f197db2303d7337e37\", \"document_keyword\": \"opentelemetry/issues/sig-security-164.md\", \"id\": \"044a41dcb622cca1\", \"image_id\": \"\", \"important_keywords\": [], \"mom_id\": \"\", \"positions\": [], \"row_id\": null, \"similarity\": 0.3666375323766416, \"tag_kwd\": [], \"term_similarity\": 0.22295516053805944, \"vector_similarity\": 0.7018964, \"dataset_name\": \"С2WR-2\", \"document_name\": \"opentelemetry/issues/sig-security-164.md\", \"document_metadata\": {\"document_id\": \"0745ef188a9c11f197db2303d7337e37\", \"name\": \"opentelemetry/issues/sig-security-164.md\", \"location\": \"opentelemetry/issues/sig-security-164.md\", \"type\": \"doc\", \"size\": 6168, \"chunk_count\": 5, \"create_date\": \"2026-07-28T23:50:16\", \"update_date\": \"2026-07-31T20:11:11\", \"token_count\": 2203, \"thumbnail\": \"\", \"dataset_id\": \"b5f5be0e8a9b11f197db2303d7337e37\", \"meta_fields\": {\"path\": \"sources\"}}}, {\"content\": \"  - Meeting notes: [Ecosystem Explorer Project](https://docs.google.com/document/d/1QBpFmSR54fGus8q6RraUj0-mEjSoX7S7fdlgsvxZsuk/edit?usp=sharing)  \\n\\n  - [https://github.com/mikeblum/otel-explorer-go-docs/blob/3797539be4f5a760e99586c0de72496019f5e6b0/instrumentation-list.yaml](https://github.com/mikeblum/otel-explorer-go-docs/blob/3797539be4f5a760e99586c0de72496019f5e6b0/instrumentation-list.yaml)  \\n\\n### SIG Security: release signing\\n\\n- Robert proposed enabling GitHub “signature releases” in addition to existing tag signing and GPG signatures of source archives.\\n\\n- Key points:\\n\\n  - GitHub’s source tarball/zip is generated at download time; signing artifacts strengthens trust and mitigates changes over time.\\n\\n  - Double-signing is acceptable and beneficial for OSS Scorecard/compliance.\\n\\n  - Constraint: Artifacts must be uploaded at release time; cannot regenerate later.\\n\\n- Decision: Proceed with enabling signature releases; update release documentation and ensure process discipline.\\n\\nReferences:\\n\\n- [https://github.com/open-telemetry/sig-security/issues/164](https://github.com/open-telemetry/sig-security/issues/164)  \\n\\n### KubeCon updates\\n\\n- OpenTelemetry Observatory booth confirmed.\\n\\n- Go SIG will meet at the booth (Tuesday morning, local time; check published schedule).\\n\\n- Plan to cancel the Zoom SIG meeting during KubeCon week; reminder will be sent next week.\\n\\n- Community encouraged to stop by the booth and participate.\\n\\n**Source ID**: [SRC-NOTE-06]\\n\\n# Meeting Note: OpenTelemetry Go SIG — 2025-11-03\\n\\n**Canonical URL**: https://github.com/open-telemetry/opentelemetry-go/issues/6648#issuecomment-3479655348  \\n\\n**Author**: pellared  \\n\\n**Created**: 2025-11-03T09:39:04Z · **Updated**: 2025-11-03T09:40:01Z  \\n\\n**Collected**: 2026-07-14T14:35:41Z\\n\\n---\\n\\n**Date:** 2025-10-30\\n\\n**Attendees:**\\n\\n- Tyler Yahn\\n\\n- Bryan Boreham\\n\\n- Damien Mathieu\\n\", \"content_ltks\": \"meet note ecosystem explor project http doc googl com document d 1qbpfmsr54fgus8q6rrauj0 mejsox7s7fdlgsvxzsuk edit usp share http github com mikeblum otel explor go doc blob 3797539be4f5a760e99586c0de72496019f5e6b0 instrument list yaml http github com mikeblum otel explor go doc blob 3797539be4f5a760e99586c0de72496019f5e6b0 instrument list yaml sig secur releas sign robert propos enabl github signatur releas in addit to exist tag sign and gpg signatur of sourc archiv key point github s sourc tarbal zip is generat at download time sign artifact strengthen trust and mitig chang over time doubl sign is accept and benefici for os scorecard complianc constraint artifact must be upload at releas time can not regener later decis proceed with enabl signatur releas updat releas document and ensur process disciplin refer http github com open telemetri sig secur issu 164 http github com open telemetri sig secur issu 164 kubecon updat opentelemetri observatori booth confirm go sig will meet at the booth tuesday morn local time check publish schedul plan to cancel the zoom sig meet dure kubecon week remind will be sent next week communiti encourag to stop by the booth and particip sourc id src note 06 meet note opentelemetri go sig 2025 11 03 canon url http github com open telemetri opentelemetri go issu 6648 issuecom 3479655348 author pellar creat 2025 11 03t09 39 04z updat 2025 11 03t09 40 01z collect 2026 07 14t14 35 41z date 2025 10 30 attende tyler yahn bryan boreham damien mathieu\", \"dataset_id\": \"b5f5be0e8a9b11f197db2303d7337e37\", \"doc_type_kwd\": \"text\", \"document_id\": \"073f05c28a9c11f197db2303d7337e37\", \"document_keyword\": \"opentelemetry/meeting-notes/entry-3479655348.md\", \"id\": \"ea6d8578d25d485e\", \"image_id\": \"\", \"important_keywords\": [], \"mom_id\": \"\", \"positions\": [], \"row_id\": null, \"similarity\": 0.3407615389779405, \"tag_kwd\": [], \"term_similarity\": 0.18044206996848644, \"vector_similarity\": 0.7148403, \"dataset_name\": \"С2WR-2\", \"document_name\": \"opentelemetry/meeting-notes/entry-3479655348.md\", \"document_metadata\": {\"document_id\": \"073f05c28a9c11f197db2303d7337e37\", \"name\": \"opentelemetry/meeting-notes/entry-3479655348.md\", \"location\": \"opentelemetry/meeting-notes/entry-3479655348.md\", \"type\": \"doc\", \"size\": 7597, \"chunk_count\": 4, \"create_date\": \"2026-07-28T23:50:16\", \"update_date\": \"2026-07-31T20:11:18\", \"token_count\": 1926, \"thumbnail\": \"\", \"dataset_id\": \"b5f5be0e8a9b11f197db2303d7337e37\", \"meta_fields\": {\"path\": \"sources\"}}}, {\"content\": \"*   David also mentioned ongoing work on exponential histograms and a simpler \\\"last value\\\" PR that shares code with the histogram one.\\n\\n*   Tyler expressed a strong desire to merge the histogram reservoir PR in the current milestone due to its significant performance improvement and encouraged attendees to review it.\\n\\n**6. Milestone Check-in and Release Goals**\\n\\n*   Tyler conducted a check-in on the v1.39.0 milestones for [Otel](https://github.com/open-telemetry/opentelemetry-go/milestone/74) and [Contrib](https://github.com/open-telemetry/opentelemetry-go-contrib/milestone/33).\\n\\n*   **Exposed Temporality Selector Function PR:** Tyler noted that a previous SIG meeting concluded this PR was API pollution and should be closed. He will draft a comment and close it today.\\n\\n*   **Simple Span Processor (Tracing):** This PR needs another round of reviews but is considered straightforward and should remain in the milestone.\\n\\n*   **OTLP Metric GRPC Exporter Metrics:** This PR has been open for a while and needs more iteration. It might be moved out of the current milestone if a release push occurs.\\n\\n*   **Metrics SDK Standard Out Metrics Exporter & Standard Log Exporter:** Both PRs lack follow-up from their original authors and significant work is still needed. They are candidates for being bumped from the milestone.\\n\\n*   **Overall Release Strategy:** Tyler proposed making a release before KubeCon (less than a month away) and urged everyone to prioritize reviews for the critical PRs to achieve this goal.\\n\\n**7. KubeCon Discussion**\\n\\n*   **David Ashpole** asked if there was anything specific to announce or discuss at KubeCon.\\n\\n*   **Robert Pająk** mentioned the extended attributes merge in specification and product as something he'd like to highlight, though it's not ready.\\n\\n*   **Tyler Yahn** expressed interest in showcasing the new observability features.\\n\\n*   David suggested working towards a stable release of the HTTP instrumentation in Contrib. Tyler agreed it was a good idea but noted the significant work involved due to existing \\\"cruft\\\" and potential needs for API restructuring.\\n\\n**8. Tyler's Side Project (OTLP Exporter Error Types)**\\n\\n*   Tyler shared that he's been working on introducing new, custom error types for OTLP exporters to provide clearer, more unified error messages. This involves distinguishing between HTTP/gRPC errors, partial errors, and warnings. He has a prototype integrated for Otel Trace gRPC. While not critical, it improves observability and user understanding of errors.\\n\", \"content_ltks\": \"david also mention ongo work on exponenti histogram and a simpler last valu pr that share code with the histogram one tyler express a strong desir to merg the histogram reservoir pr in the current mileston due to it signific perform improv and encourag attende to review it 6 mileston check in and releas goal tyler conduct a check in on the v1 39 0 mileston for otel http github com open telemetri opentelemetri go mileston 74 and contrib http github com open telemetri opentelemetri go contrib mileston 33 expos tempor selector function pr tyler note that a previous sig meet conclud this pr wa api pollut and should be close he will draft a comment and close it today simpl span processor trace this pr need anoth round of review but is consid straightforward and should remain in the mileston otlp metric grpc export metric this pr ha been open for a while and need more iter it might be move out of the current mileston if a releas push occur metric sdk standard out metric export standard log export both pr lack follow up from their origin author and signific work is still need they are candid for be bump from the mileston overal releas strategi tyler propos make a releas befor kubecon less than a month away and urg everyon to priorit review for the critic pr to achiev this goal 7 kubecon discuss david ashpol ask if there wa anyth specif to announc or discus at kubecon robert paj ą k mention the extend attribut merg in specif and product a someth he d like to highlight though it s not readi tyler yahn express interest in showcas the new observ featur david suggest work toward a stabl releas of the http instrument in contrib tyler agre it wa a good idea but note the signific work involv due to exist cruft and potenti need for api restructur 8 tyler s side project otlp export error type tyler share that he s been work on introduc new custom error type for otlp export to provid clearer more unifi error messag this involv distinguish between http grpc error partial error and warn he ha a prototyp integr for otel trace grpc while not critic it improv observ and user understand of error\", \"dataset_id\": \"b5f5be0e8a9b11f197db2303d7337e37\", \"doc_type_kwd\": \"text\", \"document_id\": \"073cfcdc8a9c11f197db2303d7337e37\", \"document_keyword\": \"opentelemetry/meeting-notes/entry-3479584781.md\", \"id\": \"1bed9e41a9b05e24\", \"image_id\": \"\", \"important_keywords\": [], \"mom_id\": \"\", \"positions\": [], \"row_id\": null, \"similarity\": 0.28499224314410326, \"tag_kwd\": [], \"term_similarity\": 0.1112926902058618, \"vector_similarity\": 0.6902912, \"dataset_name\": \"С2WR-2\", \"document_name\": \"opentelemetry/meeting-notes/entry-3479584781.md\", \"document_metadata\": {\"document_id\": \"073cfcdc8a9c11f197db2303d7337e37\", \"name\": \"opentelemetry/meeting-notes/entry-3479584781.md\", \"location\": \"opentelemetry/meeting-notes/entry-3479584781.md\", \"type\": \"doc\", \"size\": 8756, \"chunk_count\": 4, \"create_date\": \"2026-07-28T23:50:16\", \"update_date\": \"2026-07-31T20:11:19\", \"token_count\": 2164, \"thumbnail\": \"\", \"dataset_id\": \"b5f5be0e8a9b11f197db2303d7337e37\", \"meta_fields\": {\"path\": \"sources\"}}}, {\"content\": \"Can you share more about why you aren't able to migrate to the stats handler?  We [deprecated](https://github.com/open-telemetry/opentelemetry-go-contrib/pull/4534) the interceptors almost 2 years ago, which seems like plenty of time to migrate.\\n\\n---\\n\\n**nicholasngai** — 2025-10-28T20:40:37Z\\n\\nEven if we removed all of our references, references in transitive dependencies still cause compilation errors, and we don’t have control over the timeline at which transitive dependencies remove those code references.\\n\\n---\\n\\n**dmathieu** — 2025-10-29T08:35:31Z\\n\\nThat doesn't look like a good reason to me. There will always be unmaintained transitive dependencies that prevent this kind of upgrades.\\n\\nThat's tech debt that needs to be fixed, not kept on our end.\\n\\n---\\n\\n**nicholasngai** — 2025-10-29T16:28:55Z\\n\\nThe question is really whether we can rely on otelgrpc to be stable! For now, we are stuck on v0.58.0 because of compilation errors on higher versions introduced by the breaking change. If there is an urgent security patch introduced, we won’t be able to upgrade to it.\\n\\nGenerally, with Golang, we avoid breaking changes aggressively avoid these kinds of things. Does maintaining this interceptor involve significant overhead from the maintainers?\\n\\n---\\n\\n**MrAlias** — 2025-10-29T17:37:26Z\\n\\nPlease do not rely on an unstable package as being stable.\\n\\n---\\n\\n**nicholasngai** — 2025-10-29T17:38:42Z\\n\\nAre there plans to make this package stable? Or are we sticking with [ZeroVer](https://0ver.org/) for the forseeable future?\\n\\n---\\n\\n**MrAlias** — 2025-10-29T18:06:47Z\\n\\n> Are there plans to make this package stable?\\n\\nThere is definitely desire among project contributor to progress this package towards stability. But please understand this is an open-source project. It is driven by a the dedicated effort of engineers who donate their time to working on this. That time is valuable and allocated to many efforts.\\n\\nI'm happy to add the question of stabilization to our weekly SIG meeting happening tomorrow. @nicholasngai I would strongly suggest you attend the meeting tomorrow to discuss your use-case and help motivate allocation of effort for this stabilization. I don't anticipate this stabilization happening within 2025, but I could see us prioritizing it for 2026 if we have community involvement and/or added developer help here.\\n\", \"content_ltks\": \"can you share more about whi you aren t abl to migrat to the stat handler we deprec http github com open telemetri opentelemetri go contrib pull 4534 the interceptor almost 2 year ago which seem like plenti of time to migrat nicholasngai 2025 10 28t20 40 37z even if we remov all of our refer refer in transit depend still caus compil error and we don t have control over the timelin at which transit depend remov those code refer dmathieu 2025 10 29t08 35 31z that doesn t look like a good reason to me there will alway be unmaintain transit depend that prevent this kind of upgrad that s tech debt that need to be fix not kept on our end nicholasngai 2025 10 29t16 28 55z the question is realli whether we can reli on otelgrpc to be stabl for now we are stuck on v0 580 becaus of compil error on higher version introduc by the break chang if there is an urgent secur patch introduc we won t be abl to upgrad to it general with golang we avoid break chang aggress avoid these kind of thing doe maintain this interceptor involv signific overhead from the maintain mralia 2025 10 29t17 37 26z pleas do not reli on an unstabl packag a be stabl nicholasngai 2025 10 29t17 38 42z are there plan to make this packag stabl or are we stick with zerov http 0ver org for the forseeabl futur mralia 2025 10 29t18 06 47z are there plan to make this packag stabl there is definit desir among project contributor to progress this packag toward stabil but pleas understand this is an open sourc project it is driven by a the dedic effort of engin who donat their time to work on this that time is valuabl and alloc to mani effort i m happi to add the question of stabil to our week sig meet happen tomorrow nicholasngai i would strong suggest you attend the meet tomorrow to discus your use case and help motiv alloc of effort for this stabil i don t anticip this stabil happen within 2025 but i could see u priorit it for 2026 if we have communiti involv and or ad develop help here\", \"dataset_id\": \"b5f5be0e8a9b11f197db2303d7337e37\", \"doc_type_kwd\": \"text\", \"document_id\": \"0749199a8a9c11f197db2303d7337e37\", \"document_keyword\": \"opentelemetry/issues/opentelemetry-go-contrib-8078.md\", \"id\": \"11ff3d6a2e47fd9f\", \"image_id\": \"\", \"important_keywords\": [], \"mom_id\": \"\", \"positions\": [], \"row_id\": null, \"similarity\": 0.27672652665244696, \"tag_kwd\": [], \"term_similarity\": 0.08903415236063852, \"vector_similarity\": 0.7146754, \"dataset_name\": \"С2WR-2\", \"document_name\": \"opentelemetry/issues/opentelemetry-go-contrib-8078.md\", \"document_metadata\": {\"document_id\": \"0749199a8a9c11f197db2303d7337e37\", \"name\": \"opentelemetry/issues/opentelemetry-go-contrib-8078.md\", \"location\": \"opentelemetry/issues/opentelemetry-go-contrib-8078.md\", \"type\": \"doc\", \"size\": 4910, \"chunk_count\": 3, \"create_date\": \"2026-07-28T23:50:16\", \"update_date\": \"2026-07-31T20:11:06\", \"token_count\": 1517, \"thumbnail\": \"\", \"dataset_id\": \"b5f5be0e8a9b11f197db2303d7337e37\", \"meta_fields\": {\"path\": \"sources\"}}}, {\"content\": \"I don’t think this is the expected result; in any case—whether it’s middleware or something else—it should be able to retrieve the file again.\\n\\nI think we may need to investigate this issue further.\\n\\n**flc1125** on `instrumentation/github.com/gin-gonic/gin/otelgin/gin_test.go` (line 512) — 2025-11-11T13:59:33Z\\n\\nBased on this PR, I’ve provided a prototype reference: https://github.com/open-telemetry/opentelemetry-go-contrib/pull/8161\\n\\n@dmathieu @akats7, take a look and see how it works if we adjust it according to the prototype.\\n\\n**akats7** on `instrumentation/github.com/gin-gonic/gin/otelgin/gin_test.go` (line 512) — 2025-11-11T15:42:57Z\\n\\n@flc1125 can you clarify which behavior you’re referring to as incorrect, are you referring to \\n\\n```\\n\\nrequire.ErrorIs(t, err, fs.ErrNotExist)\\n\\n```\\n\\n**Yiling-J** on `instrumentation/github.com/gin-gonic/gin/otelgin/gin_test.go` (line 512) — 2025-11-12T01:28:14Z\\n\\nI thought we had already agreed on the `RemoveAll` approach? Naturally, if you call RemoveAll, the temporary files are deleted and can’t be accessed afterward. Since this happens during the middleware’s return phase, I’d expect that most middlewares wouldn’t read the multipart form at that point anyway. I’m not sure if the implications of RemoveAll were discussed in the SIG meeting, but it might be worth confirming.\\n\\n**akats7** on `instrumentation/github.com/gin-gonic/gin/otelgin/gin_test.go` (line 512) — 2025-11-12T10:24:52Z\\n\\n@flc1125 I’m still not clear on the result you’re referring to, the result aligns to my understanding of what we’ve discussed.\\n\\nAlso I’m not sure if your prototype fix would work, I think it still doesn’t address the core issue which is that when we originally set c.Request = c.Request.WithContext(ctx) with an unparsed form the http server won’t know to clean it up. I don’t think Cloning the request solves that.\\n\\n**Source ID**: [SRC-PR-01]\\n\\n# Pull Request: fix(otelgin): remove multipartform temporary file (open-telemetry/opentelemetry-go-contrib#6609)\\n\", \"content_ltks\": \"i don t think this is the expect result in ani case whether it s middlewar or someth els it should be abl to retriev the file again i think we may need to investig this issu further flc1125 on instrument github com gin gonic gin otelgin gin _ test go line 512 2025 11 11t13 59 33z base on this pr i ve provid a prototyp refer http github com open telemetri opentelemetri go contrib pull 8161 dmathieu akats7 take a look and see how it work if we adjust it accord to the prototyp akats7 on instrument github com gin gonic gin otelgin gin _ test go line 512 2025 11 11t15 42 57z flc1125 can you clarifi which behavior you re refer to a incorrect are you refer to requir errori t err f errnotexist yile j on instrument github com gin gonic gin otelgin gin _ test go line 512 2025 11 12t01 28 14z i thought we had alreadi agre on the removeal approach natur if you call removeal the temporari file are delet and can t be access afterward sinc this happen dure the middlewar s return phase i d e